    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=f(x-2)+2$.\n\nThe displacement has components 2 units right and 2 units up.",
      "worked": "Let the horizontal and vertical displacements both be $h>0$, since the translation follows $y=x$ in the direction of increasing $x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}h^2+h^2&=8\\\\2h^2&=8\\\\h^2&=4\\\\h&=2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nReplace $x$ with $x-2$ and $y$ with $y-2$:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}y-2&=f(x-2)\\\\y&=f(x-2)+2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
